; npm install scripts are default-deny in this repo, including on CI runners.
; An unapproved preinstall/postinstall fails the install with ESTRICTALLOWSCRIPTS
; instead of silently executing. npm's own default is to warn and run it anyway.
;
; Approvals live in package.json under "allowScripts", so they are committed and
; reviewable. To allow a package that genuinely needs its install step:
;
;   npm install-scripts ls              ; read the actual script text first
;   npm install-scripts approve <pkg>   ; records a pinned pkg@version entry
;   npm install-scripts prune           ; drop approvals for removed packages
;
; Why: install hooks are arbitrary code execution at install time from every
; third-party author in the tree. The Shai-Hulud worm (2026-08-04, keyv /
; cacheable, 440+ packages) delivered its credential stealer exactly that way.
;
; Do not disable this to get an install unstuck. Review and approve instead.
strict-allow-scripts=true
